| **Command**               | **What it does**                                  |
| ------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |
| `pwd`                     | Shows the current working directory.              |
| `ls`                      | Lists files and folders in the current directory. |
| `ls -l`                   | Lists files with detailed information.            |
| `ls -a`                   | Shows all files, including hidden files.          |
| `cd directory`            | Changes to the specified directory.               |
| `cd ..`                   | Moves one directory up.                           |
| `cd ~`                    | Goes to your home directory.                      |
| `mkdir folder`            | Creates a new directory.                          |
| `rmdir folder`            | Removes an empty directory.                       |
| `rm file`                 | Deletes a file.                                   |
| `rm -r folder`            | Deletes a directory and its contents.             |
| `rm -rf folder`           | Force deletes a directory and its contents.       |
| `touch file.txt`          | Creates an empty file.                            |
| `cp source destination`   | Copies files or directories.                      |
| `mv source destination`   | Moves or renames files/directories.               |
| `cat file.txt`            | Displays the contents of a file.                  |
| `less file.txt`           | Views large files one page at a time.             |
| `head file.txt`           | Shows the first 10 lines of a file.               |
| `tail file.txt`           | Shows the last 10 lines of a file.                |
| `tail -f file.txt`        | Monitors a file in real time (useful for logs).   |
| `clear`                   | Clears the terminal screen.                       |
| `history`                 | Displays previously executed commands.            |
| `echo "text"`             | Prints text to the terminal.                      |
| `echo "text" > file.txt`  | Writes text to a file (overwrites).               |
| `echo "text" >> file.txt` | Appends text to a file.                           |
| `whoami`                  | Displays the current logged-in user.              |
| `id`                      | Shows user ID (UID), group ID (GID), and groups.  |
| `hostname`                | Displays the system hostname.                     |
| `uname -a`                | Shows detailed system information.                |
| `date`                    | Displays the current date and time.               |
| `cal`                     | Displays the current month's calendar.            |


